{
  "_doc": "The animated background vocabulary, shared by the three engines. A background is a PURE FUNCTION of time: paint(ctx_or_array, w, h, t, params) draws frame t from nothing, so any t renders the same frame on any machine, at any fps, with no accumulated state. Geometry is normalised to the frame box (fractions of w/h), and every colour is a BRAND ROLE resolved by the renderer — no hex ever appears in a pattern. Implementation: lib/backgrounds.js (K and R share one file) and procedural-reels/backgrounds.py (P). tests/test_backgrounds.py fails if any of the three drifts from this file.",
  "version": 2,
